        </item>
        <item>
         <layout class="QVBoxLayout" name="about_categories_layout">
          <property name="spacing">
           <number>6</number>
          </property>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_categories_title_label">
            <property name="font">
             <font>
              <bold>true</bold>
             </font>
            </property>
            <property name="text">
             <string>About the number of categories</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
          <item>
           <widget class="QLabel" name="about_categories_label">
            <property name="text">
             <string>&lt;b&gt;Automatic classification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Snooz fits Gaussian mixtures of 1, 2, 3 and 4 components to the distribution of the transition frequencies.&lt;br/&gt;• It keeps the mixture with the lowest Akaike information criterion (AIC), the one that fits best. The AIC weighs the fit against the number of components.&lt;br/&gt;• The number of components of this mixture is the number of categories in the data.&lt;br/&gt;• The log of the run lists the AIC of each mixture. The picture saved in the output folder shows them.&lt;br/&gt;&lt;br/&gt;&lt;b&gt;Manual classification&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;• Snooz fits one Gaussian mixture, with the number of categories you set as its number of components.&lt;br/&gt;• Useful when the automatic classification does not analyze your data correctly, or when you already know the number of categories in the data.&lt;br/&gt;• For example, classify the whole cohort automatically to find the number of categories. Then set this number to classify each subject, if you also analyze the subjects one by one.</string>
            </property>
            <property name="textFormat">
             <enum>Qt::TextFormat::RichText</enum>
            </property>
            <property name="wordWrap">
             <bool>true</bool>
            </property>
            <property name="variant" stdset="0">
             <string notr="true">help</string>
            </property>
           </widget>
          </item>
         </layout>
        </item>
